---- (e2) codimension-3 fold test.
     For a triple root the local solution space at z=1/8 is spanned by
     y1^3, y1^2 y2, y1 y2^2, y2^3 with y2 = y1 log(1-8z) + hol.  A combination
     has radius 1/4 (i.e. |u_n|^(1/n) -> 4) iff it is log-FREE at z=1/8, i.e.
     iff c_{0,2} = c_{0,1} = c_{0,0} = 0 -- THREE conditions on the six
     sequences A = X^(0), X^(1),...,X^(5).  Real kernel is 3-dimensional;
     the question is whether it contains a rational point.

